    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07352b2c_7ed90640",
        "filename": "graphics/mapper/4.0/IMapper.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1073546
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-28T16:49:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The normal HIDL extension process allows types to be extended. A vendor extension to a HIDL extension looks exactly the same as when Google does a minor rev on an interface. So a good example of how it would look is android.hardware.graphics.common@1.1\u0027s PixelFormat which extends the 1.0 PixelFormat.",
      "parentUuid": "e42a8f0c_bc7bcce8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "4e8054dac6e39851a1ac9d205424d3496ed29029",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b972d4f2_cd5237b4",
        "filename": "graphics/mapper/4.0/IMapper.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1468456
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-28T21:17:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that mechanism is a hassle to work with when all you need to pass in is an int :(\n\nfor RenderIntents -  we can use a vendor specific range - http://androidxref.com/9.0.0_r3/xref/hardware/interfaces/graphics/common/1.1/types.hal#291\n\ncan we use the same thing here?",
      "parentUuid": "07352b2c_7ed90640",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "4e8054dac6e39851a1ac9d205424d3496ed29029",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
